# Counts past what 16 bits hold, end to end (#2336, CR 122.1, 120.3, 107.1: nothing caps a counter, a creature's size or damage).
# Doubling Season (CR 614.1a: twice that many counters are put instead) is in play when Mossborn Hydra enters, so it enters with 2
# +1/+1 counters, and each landfall "double the number of +1/+1 counters" (CR 701.10e) puts N more, which Doubling Season doubles
# to 2N: the counters triple. Five Wooded Foothills played over five turns and then all fetching a Forest make ten
# landfalls: 2 x 3^10 = 118,098 counters, past 32,767 after the ninth (39,366). The 118,098/118,098 trampler then attacks Bot2
# unblocked and deals 118,098, past 65,535: Bot2 is at 20 - 118,098 = -118,078 and has lost.

